From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rockchip: sai: re-apply the SDO/SDI routing on resume

A non-default rockchip,sai-tx-route never reaches the hardware. The
routing is programmed once, from rockchip_sai_parse_paths() during
probe, and by the time the device is running SAI_PATH_SEL has returned
to its reset value. The regcache sync in the resume path does not
restore it either, so the property is silently ignored and the stream
leaves on whichever SDO port the reset mapping selects.

This is invisible on every board in tree, because they all describe the
identity mapping (<0 1 2 3>) that the register already holds after
reset -- writing it and losing the write are indistinguishable. It is
only visible on a board whose codec sits on an SDO port other than the
one the reset mapping drives, where the card streams correctly, every
clock and pin reads correct, and the output is silent.

Program the routing from rockchip_sai_runtime_resume() instead, after
the cache sync, so it is established whenever the device is powered
rather than once at probe. When no route is described the values are
the reset mapping, so the write is a no-op.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
index ed393e503..15a3aafcf 100644
--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
@@ -248,6 +248,9 @@ static int rockchip_sai_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void rockchip_sai_path_config(struct rk_sai_dev *sai,
+				     int num, bool is_rx);
+
 static int rockchip_sai_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct rk_sai_dev *sai = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
@@ -267,6 +270,16 @@ static int rockchip_sai_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_regmap;
 
+	/*
+	 * Re-apply the DT-described SDO/SDI routing. The probe-time write in
+	 * rockchip_sai_parse_paths() does not survive to the running device,
+	 * and the cache sync above does not restore SAI_PATH_SEL to it either,
+	 * so a non-default route is silently lost. Writing it here also keeps
+	 * it across every runtime-PM cycle rather than only at probe.
+	 */
+	rockchip_sai_path_config(sai, sai->tx_lanes, false);
+	rockchip_sai_path_config(sai, sai->rx_lanes, true);
+
 	return 0;
 
 err_regmap:
-- 
2.43.0

